class:: SyncModeOsc
summary:: Bandlimited oscillator with six explicit synchronization laws
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

SyncModeOsc applies one of six synchronization laws to a signed phase
accumulator. Sine, BLAMP triangle, BLEP saw, and BLEP pulse shapes share the
same event engine. Abrupt synchronization jumps receive a short causal
correction, and sync edges are always processed before a simultaneous local
wrap.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/SyncSaw::. SyncSaw implements a
master/slave reset relationship; SyncModeOsc accepts an arbitrary trigger and
can reset, reverse, flip, pull, arm, or hold its phase.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed local frequency in hertz.

argument:: sync
Trigger or gate input. Modes code::0..4:: detect nonpositive-to-positive
edges; mode code::5:: holds phase while the value is positive.

argument:: mode
Initialization-rate law: code::0:: hard reset, code::1:: reverse,
code::2:: half-cycle flip, code::3:: soft pull, code::4:: reset at the next
local wrap, or code::5:: hold.

argument:: resetPhase
Target phase in cycles, wrapped to code::0..1::.

argument:: symmetry
Triangle breakpoint or pulse width, clamped to code::0.02..0.98::.

argument:: shape
Initialization-rate waveform: code::0:: sine, code::1:: triangle,
code::2:: saw, or code::3:: pulse.

argument:: softness
Soft-pull duration in seconds, clamped to code::0..10::.

argument:: oversample
Initialization-rate factor code::1::, code::2::, or code::4::.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier.

argument:: add
Offset added after multiplication.

returns::
One audio signal.

method:: kr

SyncModeOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

Soft pull divides the shortest wrapped phase difference into an exact finite
number of samples. Armed reset fires once. Hold resumes from the unchanged
phase. Causal jump correction preserves event timing and reduces, but cannot
eliminate, hard-sync aliasing.

examples::

code::
(
{ SyncModeOsc.ar(110, Impulse.ar(37), 0, shape: 2) * 0.07 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    SyncModeOsc.ar(
        58, Impulse.ar(LFNoise1.kr(0.2).exprange(3, 70)),
        mode: 3, resetPhase: 0.25,
        symmetry: LFNoise1.kr(0.1).range(0.1, 0.9),
        shape: 3, softness: 0.03, oversample: 4
    ) * 0.065;
}.play;
)
::

